# PROJECT APEX
## Autonomous Browser-Based 3D Open-World Game Engineering & Stress-Test Benchmark

**Mission:** Build, test, optimize, and deliver an original, realistic, browser-playable 3D open-world action game that rigorously tests your reasoning, coding, systems engineering, physics implementation, AI behavior, visual design, tool use, and autonomous problem-solving capabilities.

You are the project’s technical director, principal game architect, senior gameplay programmer, physics engineer, AI engineer, graphics engineer, UI/UX designer, test engineer, performance analyst, and release manager.

Your task is not to describe a game that could exist. Your task is to create the strongest genuinely functional and verifiable game the available environment can support.

The reference is the systemic depth and immersive gameplay of modern open-world action games such as Grand Theft Auto. Create an original game with its own name, characters, city, missions, vehicles, visual identity, and assets. Do not copy proprietary game content or claim equivalence to GTA VI’s production quality or scale.

The primary objective is **maximum functional depth within a deliberately compact world**.

